# RideAtlas workflow

## Releases
- Bump `lib/build_info.dart` (`kAppBuildLabel` + `kAppBuildNote`) and add a matching entry at the top of `lib/changelog.dart` on every user-facing push to `main`.
- Web update versioning is automatic: deploy-web.yml stamps `web/sw.js` `APP_VERSION`, `web/index.html` `RIDEATLAS_WEB_VERSION` and the `?v=` cache busters from `kAppBuildLabel` on every deploy. Do not hand-edit those version strings; do not add a second web update UI (bottom banner only, no header icon).
- Prefer **one product change per version**. Do not ship a product version solely for CI/toolchain bumps.
- Infra-only fixes (Gradle/AGP/Kotlin/CI): bump toolchain in **one** commit; mention briefly in the product note only if users must reinstall, otherwise keep the note product-focused.

## Git
- Prefer **squash merge** (or a single commit) into `main` instead of feature+merge pairs that double history noise.
- Do not force-push `main`.

## Before pushing Android changes
- Prefer a **local** `build_apk.bat` / `flutter build apk --release` when Flutter is available, then sideload-test screen-off recording if GPS/background code changed.
- If Flutter is unavailable on this machine, say so and rely on CI — do not invent a local binary path.
- Do **not** build from a Google Drive / OneDrive synced path; use a local clone (e.g. `C:\src\RideAtlas` / `C:\src\RideAtlas-dev`). Sync folders often mark dirs ReadOnly and break `lib/l10n` + plugin symlinks.

## Product / UI discipline
- Decide the screen/layout **once** before implementing. Avoid add-then-remove thrash (e.g. a second summary page that duplicates Analysis).
- For GPS/map bugs: state a hypothesis, change **one** mechanism, then verify — do not stack interval + animation + provider switches in the same version without a clear root cause.

## Android background GPS
- Recording on Android uses the **native** `RecordingLocationService` foreground service. Do not reintroduce Dart-only `Geolocator.getPositionStream` as the sole recorder for Android screen-off.
